<section class="section section--flush-top">
  <div class="container split">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">The closed loop</p>
      <h2>Where detection meets verification.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Finding a leak is the first half. Assetas closes the other half: every finding automatically becomes owned work until the fix is proven and emissions are accounted.</p>
      <p>Log a leak and the follow-up chain is created automatically — repair task, retest, and verification, each with an owner, a due date, and a traceable history. A failed retest reopens the loop; a passed one closes it with evidence attached.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Auto-created follow-ups</strong> the moment a leak is logged or a repair fails retest.</li>
        <li><strong>Deadlines tracked per rule —</strong> first-attempt and final-repair clocks visible on the record.</li>
        <li><strong>Delay of Repair handled properly:</strong> justification, extension history, and timeline attached to the same record.</li>
        <li><strong>Verification can't be skipped —</strong> the record stays open until the loop is closed.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
